# ── (Removed) legacy redirect shim for old API paths ──────────────────────────
# A previous version of this file rewrote old function paths to /api/* with a
# 200-status rewrite. Cloudflare Pages doesn't reliably proxy POST requests
# through that kind of rewrite (confirmed live: it returned a bare 405 with
# no body instead of forwarding the request — that's what broke the AI
# article button, escrow release, and withdrawal requests). All frontend code
# now calls /api/payment, /api/ai-generate, /api/sitemap-dynamic etc. directly,
# so no shim is needed — deleting it instead of leaving a trap for the next
# edit that forgets and calls an old path again.
# /sitemap-live.xml is now served directly by functions/sitemap-live.xml.js
# (the old 200-rewrite to /api/sitemap-dynamic returned 404 on Pages).

# Blog routes
