# Legacy standalone legal pages.
#
# ⚠️ FIXED (audit finding): the project shipped TWO different policies for the
# same document, and the redirect pointed the newer one at the older one:
#     terms.html   (standalone, "آخر تحديث: أغسطس 2026",  8 sections)
#     privacy.html (standalone, "آخر تحديث: أغسطس 2026",  7 sections)
#     terms/index.html   (folder, "آخر تحديث: 21 مايو 2025", 13 sections)
#     privacy/index.html (folder, "آخر تحديث: 21 мая 2025", 10 sections)
# So the 2026 text was unreachable, and two contradicting legal documents sat in
# the same deploy with no way for anyone to tell which one governs.
#
# Resolved by keeping the folder versions as the single canonical source — they
# are the more complete of the two — and DELETING the two standalone duplicates.
# Nothing in the project ever linked to /terms.html or /privacy.html: every
# footer, the signup modal and all blog pages link to /terms and /privacy
# directly. These two 301s are kept purely so old bookmarks, backlinks and URLs
# already indexed by Google still land on the live policy instead of a 404.
/terms.html /terms 301
/privacy.html /privacy 301

